\p
\v 1 To¦155907 the¦155907 assembly's¦155914 messenger¦155908 in¦155911 Ephesus¦155912 write¦155915:
\p The¦155918 one holding¦155919 the seven stars¦155922 in his¦155926 right¦155925 hand¦155925, the one walking¦155929 among the seven golden¦155936 lampstands¦155934, says¦155917 these \add things\add*:
\v 2 “I know¦155937 about¦155940 your activities and work¦155939, and your endurance¦155947 and that you can't¦155951 tolerate evil¦155954 people, and that you've investigated the¦155958 ones who call themselves¦155961 missionaries¦155963 but¦155941 are¦155967 not¦155951, and you've found¦155969 them¦155970 to¦155961 be¦155961 frauds.
\v 3 \add I'm aware that\add* you've endured¦155975 and¦155974 even suffered \add persecution\add* because¦155982 you've \add believed in\add* me¦155985, but¦155974 you've never given up.
\v 4 However, I do have something against¦155994 you: you've abandoned the¦155997 love¦155998 that¦155996 you first¦156001 had.
\v 5 So¦156019 \add now, you need to\add* remember¦156006 where¦156008 you've¦156009 fallen¦156009 from, and repent and repeat how you behaved at the¦156014 beginning, but¦156019 if you don't, I'll come¦156021 to you and if you don't repent, I'll remove¦156026 your¦156029 lampstand¦156028 from its¦156033 place¦156032.
\v 6 But¦156037 you do have¦156040 this¦156038 going for you: you hate what the¦156043 \add disciples of\add* Nicolaus are¦156040 doing,\f + \fr 2:7 \ft Nicolaus' disciples ate food that had been sacrificed to idols and committed sexual sins.\f* just¦156038 like I do.
\p
\v 7 Everyone who wants¦156051 to understand¦156051 needs¦156053 to listen¦156053 to what¦156054 \add God's\add* \nd spirit¦156056\nd* is¦156057 saying¦156057 to the¦156058 assemblies¦156060.
\p I will¦156065 grant \add the right\add* to eat¦156067 from the¦156069 tree¦156070 \add that gives\add* life¦156072 in¦156075 God's paradise¦156079 to everyone who overcomes¦156064.”\x + \xo 2:7: a \xt Gen 2:9; Rev 22:2; \xo b \xt Eze 28:13; 31:8 (LXX).\x*
