\p The¦156088 one who's¦156103 the¦156097 first¦156099 and¦156084 the¦156101 last¦156102, who died¦156105 but¦156084 lived¦156107 \add again\add*, says¦156096 these things:
\v 9 “I know about your suffering and¦156115 your poverty¦156117, but you're¦156121 \add actually\add* rich¦156119! I also¦156115 know how about the¦156123 slander¦156124 of¦156126 those who consider themselves¦156132 to¦156131 be¦156131 Jews, but they're¦156135 not¦156134 \add true\add* Jews because \add ≈their master is\add* Satan¦156139.
\v 10 Don't be afraid¦156142 about¦156154 what¦156143 you're¦156144 going¦156144 to¦156146 suffer¦156146. Yes, the¦156152 devil¦156153 will throw¦156150 some¦156150 of¦156154 you into¦156158 prison¦156159 where your¦156154 \add faith\add* will be tested¦156161, and you'll experience persecution for¦156167 ten¦156168 days¦156167. \add Just\add* remain faithful¦156170, even if it means death¦156172, and I'll¦156174 give¦156174 you life¦156179 as a reward.
