\p The¦156203 one with the¦156216 sharp¦156217 sword¦156213 says¦156209 these things:
\v 13 “I know¦156218 where you live: where Satan's¦156229 throne¦156227 is¦156229. Despite that, you firmly \add believe in me\add* and¦156236 you haven't denied¦156238 your faith¦156240 in me, even¦156242 when Antipas¦156249, the¦156253 faithful¦156254 \add man who told others about me\add* was¦156257 killed¦156257 in your \add city\add*, where Satan lives.
\v 14 But¦156296 I do have a few¦156269 things against¦156267 you: you have some¦156271 people there¦156273 who¦156278 hold¦156274 to \add the ancient prophet\add* Balaam's¦156277 teaching.\x + \xo 2:14: a \xt Num 22:5,7; 31:16; Deu 23:4; \xo b \xt Num 25:1-3.\x* He taught¦156276 \add Moab's king\add*, Balak¦156284, how to tempt¦156288 the Israelis¦156292 and to eat¦156294 \add food\add* that had been sacrificed¦156295 to idols¦156295, and to be sexually¦156297 immoral¦156297.
