\v 1 To¦156638 the¦156650 assembly's¦156643 messenger¦156639 in¦156641 Sardis¦156642 write¦156645:
\p The¦156648 one having¦156649 the seven spirits¦156652 of \nd God¦156654\nd* and the seven stars¦156658 says¦156647 these things: “I know¦156659 what you're achieving and that¦156663 you have¦156659 a reputation¦156665 of being ‘alive’, but¦156637 you're \add actually\add* dead¦156670.
\v 2 So wake up \add from the dead\add* and strengthen¦156675 what's left and was about¦156687 to¦156683 die¦156683, because¦156685 your¦156687 actions have¦156686 been¦156690 inadequate in \nd God's¦156693\nd* sight.
\v 3 Remember¦156695 how you \add first\add* listened to and internalised \add God's message\add*, and how you obeyed it¦156702 and repented¦156704. If¦156706 you don't¦156708 wake up \add soon\add*, I'll come \add unexpectedly\add*—you'll certainly not¦156718 know¦156719 \add in advance\add* when I'll be¦156724 coming.\x + \xo 3:3: \xt Mat 24:43-44; Luk 12:39-40; Rev 16:15.\x*
\v 4 But¦156742 you¦156728 do have¦156728 a few¦156729 people in Sardis¦156734 who¦156735 haven't stained their¦156741 records, and because¦156750 they are¦156728 worthy¦156751, they'll¦156743 \add be\add* dressed in white¦156749 and walk¦156743 with¦156746 me¦156747.
\v 5 \add So\add* anyone who conquers will¦156757 be¦156757 dressed like that in¦156759 \add pure\add* white¦156761, and I certainly won't¦156764 erase their names from¦156769 the¦156766 Book of¦156768 Life¦156773, but¦156762 I'll¦156765 declare their names to my¦156784 father¦156783 and to his¦156768 messengers¦156788.\x + \xo 3:5: a \xt Exo 32:32-33; Psa 69:28; Rev 20:12; \xo b \xt Mat 10:32; Luk 12:8.\x*
