\v 11 I'll come¦156950 quickly¦156951. Hold¦156952 firmly to what¦156953 you¦156954 have¦156954 so that¦156955 no¦156956 one¦156956 can take¦156957 away your¦156960 crown¦156959.
\v 12 Anyone who's an overcomer¦156962, I'll¦156963 make¦156963 them a pillar¦156966 in¦156967 my god's temple¦156969 and they'll never¦156976 leave it again. I will write¦156981 my god's name on¦156982 them, and the name of my god's city¦156993 (the new Jerusalem which will come¦156978 down¦157002 out¦157003 of heaven¦157005 from¦157006 my god), and my new name.\x + \xo 3:12: a \xt Rev 21:2; \xo b \xt Isa 62:2; 65:15.\x*
\p
\v 13 Everyone who wants¦157017 to understand¦157017 needs¦157019 to listen¦157019 to what¦157020 \add God's\add* \nd spirit¦157022\nd* is¦157023 saying¦157023 to the¦157024 assemblies¦157025.”
\s1 The message to the assembly in Laodicea
\rem /s1 The Message to the Church in Laodicea
\p
